#heading(level: 3)[#text("Availability, selling and crafting")]
#text("These prices assume a supplied town. Ordinary travel goods are common. Specialist") #text("tools, potions and unusual supplies need an appropriate seller. Special equipment") #text("prices are valuation benchmarks: the DA decides whether an item is actually on") #text("sale. No automatic stock refresh after a rest or new scene.")

#text("For an unusual shortage or remote seller, the DA may quote double ordinary prices;") #text("otherwise use the printed value rather than maintaining regional multipliers.") #text("Record a concrete offer before buying. Exact scarcity and merchant stock remain") #text("adventure decisions, not a universal cap on player purchases.")

#text("")#strong[#text("Agreed sale/trade rule:")]#text(" intact, useful gear sells for half list price,") #text("rounded down, or trades for its full listed value with a willing trader. A 12-coin weapon sells for 6 coins or trades for 12 coins of goods. Pay any shortfall in coins; unused trade value is not cash change. A trade cannot be redeemed for coins, vouchers or other cash equivalents at full value. Card-granted items use the same rule, and selling") #text("never renews their grant. Consumables and materials with uncertain remaining supply") #text("have no standard resale offer. Goods freshly crafted or acquired at full supply") #text("may attract half-price offers, but the buyer must actually need that quantity.") #text("Special items still require an available willing trader; apply the same half-sale/full-trade rule to the agreed item valuation. Treasure such as gems has its stated") #text("trade value, without a second automatic half-price reduction.")

#text("All material bundles must name their actual contents. Ordinary d6 ingredients") #text("cost 12 coins; a d6 prepared healing-ingredient bundle costs 80. Other rare inputs") #text("need a quote. Materials must meet the recipe: a common bundle cannot become life") #text("salts by relabeling it. Recipes are still found, derived or granted through cards,") #text("not automatically available for coin purchase.")

#text("Crafting remains useful. Gathering ingredients, knowing recipes and spending time") #text("can save coins. Foraging success,") #text("recipe yields, local demand and available downtime determine profit. A merchant’s") #text("willing purchase is not an infinite exchange machine. Discuss large commercial projects with the DA before assuming guaranteed income.")

